From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vmwgfx: declare the premultiplied blend mode on all planes

Linux 7.3 warns for every plane that exposes a pixel format with alpha
but has no blend mode property:

  vmwgfx 0000:00:0f.0: [drm] [PLANE:38:plane-0] pixel format with alpha
  exposed but blend mode not setup. Please fix.

The vmwgfx primary and cursor planes offer ARGB formats. Create the
blend mode property with only DRM_MODE_BLEND_PREMULTI, the blending the
driver already uses and the DRM default for planes without the
property, so behaviour does not change.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vmwgfx/vmwgfx_kms.c	2026-09-20 22:48:15.000000000 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vmwgfx/vmwgfx_kms.c	2026-09-26 10:08:22.548104723 +0200
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 
 #include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
+#include <drm/drm_blend.h>
 #include <drm/drm_damage_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fourcc.h>
 #include <drm/drm_rect.h>
@@ -1185,6 +1186,18 @@
 		if (ret) /* Fallback */
 			ret = vmw_kms_ldu_init_display(dev_priv);
 	}
+	if (!ret) {
+		struct drm_plane *plane;
+
+		/*
+		 * The primary and cursor planes offer formats with alpha. Declare
+		 * the premultiplied blending they already use, so the DRM core
+		 * does not warn that the blend mode is not set up.
+		 */
+		drm_for_each_plane(plane, dev)
+			drm_plane_create_blend_mode_property(plane,
+							     BIT(DRM_MODE_BLEND_PREMULTI));
+	}
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(display_unit_names) != (vmw_du_max + 1));
 	drm_info(&dev_priv->drm, "%s display unit initialized\n",
 		 display_unit_names[dev_priv->active_display_unit]);
